 Plane - The single geometric plane in which transverse wave particle oscillations (ric/magnetic fields in electromagnetic waves) are restricted.


 Annihilation - The process of a particle and its anti-particle colliding and 
                being converted into energy. The energy is released into  
                2 photons to conserve. 

 Pair Production - The process of a sufficiently high-energy photon converting into 
                   a particle and its corresponding antiparticle.  Photons - Discrete(fixed) packets of EM radiation called quanta. 


 Rest Mass - The mass of the particle where it is at rest. 

 Rest Energy - The energy of a particle due to its rest mass. 

 ElectronVolt - The energy of an electron when it moves in a P.D of 1V. 


Strong nuclear force - The fundamental force that binds quarks together and holds nucleon(protons and neutrons) within a nucleus. Range 0.3 - 0.5 femtometers 

Electromagnetic force - The fundamental force that acts between all electrically charged particles and posesses infinite range. 

Weak interaction force - Responsible for particle decay and quarks flavours. It has an extremely short range. 

gravitational force - It is the weakest of the 4 fundamental forces of nature yet it has infinite range. Its exchange particle, the graviton 
                      has not been proven. 

exchange particles - Short-lived virtual particles that carry energy, momentum and forces between matter particles.


